● Not a live bug. The bot didn't trace the call graph.

  Both production callers explicitly filter SW-only layers before invoking xfer_gof:

  - h/tron/models/model.hpp:1729 (gof_rodeo_impl):
  // SW-only layers carry no HBM allocation; xfer_gof would deref null bases.
  if (!self_attn_state.hw_attn_cfg.layer_uses_hw(layer)) return;
  - with the comment that literally describes the failure mode the bot is "discovering."
  - src/tron/gof.cpp:129 (backfill_shard):
  for (size_t layer = 0; layer < gl->gofs.size(); ++layer) {
    if (!params.layer_uses_hw(layer)) continue;
    ...
    sh->xfer_gof(*g, ...);
  }

  So in actual usage today, xfer_gof never receives a SW-only layer — the precondition is enforced by callers. The shard ctor's "skip and zero" behavior at
  gof.cpp:30-32 is exactly the symmetric agreement: SW-only layers get {0, 0, 0} and aren't touched by either ctor's allocation path, the dtor's free_kv_weights
  (also guarded by layer_alloc_bytes == 0 at gof.cpp:48), or the DMA path.

