```

this is left over from evolution, after I had to start supporting gpt-oss heads that are only 64 wide. It's actually _correct_ for a true head-64-native slot layout (which we don't have today). The only production caller today passes HW_BAKED_HEAD_SIZE as that parameter, with a note (below):
```
  // DMA size and stride follow the bitfile's HBM layout (HW_BAKED_HEAD_SIZE),
  // not the model's kv_head_size. When the two differ the upper cells
  // are zero-padded by the cacheblock's pre-cleared backing buffer.
  return xfer_k_packed_entry(dev, position_ptr(position & 0x3, 0), position,
      params->n_kv_heads, fpga_index, hbm_addr, HW_BAKED_HEAD_SIZE, layer, readback);
```

The other uses are UT cases, which go through `xfer_k_entry` to get here, and _that_ function is not a production-reachable function. It's basically just a test function. We really should go back and improve our documentation I suppose. Either way, this particular utility is parameterized intentionally.
